{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=Egan&limit=10&title=The Devil's Element","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"titleInfo":[{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"devil's element","subTitle":"phosphorus and a world out of balance"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Phosphorus and a world out of balance"}],"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Egan, Dan","role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author."}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"code","@authority":"marcrelator","#text":"aut"}}]},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Informational works"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Informational works"},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Documents d'information."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2023"},"edition":"First edition.","issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York, NY :"}},"publisher":"W.W. Norton & Company,","dateIssued":[2023]}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xxvii, 228 pages ; 24 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"The story of phosphorus spans the globe and vast tracts of human history. The race to mine phosphorus took people from the battlefields of Waterloo, which were looted for the bones of fallen soldiers, to the fabled guano islands off Peru, the Bone Valley of Florida, and the sand dunes of the Western Sahara. Over the past century, phosphorus has made farming vastly more productive, feeding the enormous increase in the human population. Yet, as the author harrowingly reports, our overreliance on this vital crop nutrient is causing toxic algae blooms and \"dead zones\" in waterways from the coasts of Florida to the Mississippi River basin to the Great Lakes and beyond. This book also explores the alarming reality that diminishing access to phosphorus poses a threat to the food system worldwide-- which risks rising conflict and even war.--"},"tableOfContents":"Note to readers -- Introduction -- Part I. The race for phosphorus: 1. The devil's element -- 2. The circle of life, broken -- 3. Bones to stones -- 4. War of the sands. -- Part II. The cost of phosphorus: 5. Dirty soap -- 6. Toxic water -- 7. Empty beaches -- 8. A liquid heart, diseased. -- Part III. The future of phosphorus: 9. Waste not. -- Acknowledgments -- Notes -- Partial bibliography -- Index.","targetAudience":{"@authority":"marctarget","#text":"adult"},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Dan Egan."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Phosphorus","Environmental aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Phosphorus in agriculture","Environmental aspects"]},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Phosphorus"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Phosphates"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Pollutants"},{"@authority":"lcshac","topic":["Phosphorous","Environmental aspects"]},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Phosphorus"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Phosphates"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Harmful Algal Bloom"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Environmental Pollutants"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Phosphore","Aspect de l'environnement"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Phosphore en agriculture","Aspect de l'environnement"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Phosphore"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Phosphates"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Polluants"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"pollutants"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / Chemistry / Environmental"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"NATURE / Ecology"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SCIENCE / History"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING / Agriculture / Agronomy / Crop Science"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Phosphorus","Environmental aspects"]}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"QH545.P5 E43 2023"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"QH 545.P5"},{"@edition":"23/eng/20230206","@authority":"ddc","#text":"577/.14"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781324002666"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1324002662"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781324074724"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"1324074728"},{"@type":"isbn","@invalid":"yes","#text":"9781324002673"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"2023947185"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"1370349936"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/99156657651003941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"QH545.P5 E43 2023"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000041937001X","#text":"Francis A. Countway Library of Medicine"},"shelfLocator":"QH 545.P5 E28d 2023"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Countway Medicine","Widener"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/99156657651003941","processingDate":"2025-06-13T01:06Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"rda","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"NjBwBT"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":